# testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime (ir/AOTEffectsNet.h, SecondLaneInEffectsNet) takes a second word of digests of each operand, for the heaps that the first word has no lane for.
# f6 = the arrow function in makeCounter
# RUN(NET): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all
# NET: 7
# NET-NEXT: 2
# NET-NEXT: 1
# NET-NEXT: 18
# NET-NEXT: went on
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects: one effects entry is treated as if it did not write one heap.
# RUN(BYTES): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/%TypedArray%.prototype.fill/TypedArrayElements mechanisms=all
# BYTES: say that the call does not write TypedArrayElements, but these parts of operand {{*}} changed: the bytes
# BYTES-NOT: went on
# BYTES: crashed
# BYTES: with
# RUN(REGEXP): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/RegExp.prototype.exec/RegExpState mechanisms=all
# REGEXP: say that the call does not write RegExpState, but these parts of operand {{*}} changed: the RegExp state
# REGEXP-NOT: went on
# REGEXP: crashed
# REGEXP: with
# RUN(PROTOTYPE): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Object.setPrototypeOf/PrototypeLinks mechanisms=all
# PROTOTYPE: say that the call does not write PrototypeLinks, but these parts of operand {{*}} changed: the prototype
# PROTOTYPE-NOT: went on
# PROTOTYPE: crashed
# PROTOTYPE: with
